From 988751b0560ecd39e6e526aba63e4c46e63138b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:24:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] Noah-MP: move truncated thin snow to the soil instead
 of deleting it

Noah-MP sets snow without layers to zero when snowh <= 1e-6 m or
sneqv <= 1e-3 mm (energy, snowh2o, and the end of noahmp_sflx), and the water
goes nowhere. Ice dripping off the canopy (precip_heat) reaches the ground as
~1e-4 mm of snowfall per step, so on snow-free ground snowh2o deleted it every
step; Noah-MP's own water check (errwat) saw the loss but nothing acts on it.

Add the truncated snow to the top soil layer as ice, as snowh2o already does
with excess sublimation. Snow with layers is unchanged.

Measured with in-model meters (C96 control_p8_ugwpv1, 24 h, 1.77M soil
column-steps): errwat summed to -15.6 mm, all of it in this truncation (snowh2o
moved 15.60 mm in 124,000 events; energy 0.02 mm; end of noahmp_sflx none).
With the fix errwat sums to -0.014 mm (round-off), every column-step is below
1e-4 mm, and the land balance per call closes to 0.00000 mm per 6 h.

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
---
 physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90 | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90 b/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
index b82a541f..e72b0673 100644
--- a/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
+++ b/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
@@ -945,6 +945,8 @@ contains
     end if
 
     if(snowh <= 1.e-6 .or. sneqv <= 1.e-3) then
+     ! the truncated snow goes to the top soil layer as ice
+     if(isnow == 0) smc(1) = smc(1) + sneqv/(dzsnso(1)*1000.)
      snowh = 0.0
      sneqv = 0.0
     end if
@@ -2047,6 +2049,8 @@ endif   ! croptype == 0
 
      fsno = 0.
      if(snowh <= 1.e-6 .or. sneqv <= 1.e-3) then
+       ! the truncated snow goes to the top soil layer as ice
+       if(isnow == 0) smc(1) = smc(1) + sneqv/(dzsnso(1)*1000.)
        snowh = 0.0
        sneqv = 0.0
      end if
@@ -8178,6 +8182,8 @@ zolmax = xkrefsqr / sqrt(xkzo)   ! maximum z/L
    end if
 
    if(snowh <= 1.e-6 .or. sneqv <= 1.e-3) then
+     ! the truncated snow goes to the top soil layer as ice
+     if(isnow == 0) sice(1) = sice(1) + sneqv/(dzsnso(1)*1000.)
      snowh = 0.0
      sneqv = 0.0
    end if
